2. Additional terms for the TianShu secondary-development portions
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The TianShu authors have performed **substantial modifications** on top of
the DeerFlow upstream to deliver a multi-tenant, fully-isolated,
enterprise-oriented agent workbench (see README.md for the list of new
features and changes). These TianShu-specific modifications, additions, and
derivative works are:

  (a) Released only for **personal learning, research, and non-commercial**
      evaluation. You may download, build, run, study, and modify the source
      code on your own machine for personal, non-commercial purposes only.

  (b) **Commercial use is NOT permitted** under this license. "Commercial
      use" includes, without limitation:
        - using the software (or any modified version) to provide any
          product or service to third parties, whether or not for a fee;
        - integrating the software (in whole or in part) into any
          commercial product, SaaS offering, or internal production
          service that supports the operations of a for-profit
          organization;
        - selling, hosting-as-a-service, or charging for access to the
          software or any service built on top of it.

  (c) If you wish to use this project (or any modified version of it) for
      any commercial purpose, **you must obtain a separate written
      commercial license from the TianShu authors first**. Please contact
      the maintainers to discuss licensing terms.

  (d) The attribution and copyright notices above, the link to the
      upstream DeerFlow project, and these additional terms must be kept
      intact in all copies or substantial portions of the software.

  (e) The upstream DeerFlow MIT terms above continue to apply to all
